('APX-S-4194-1', 'APX-C-4194', 1, null, null, null, 'Please generate a high-completion, high-definition ''Street Freestyle Football 16-Step Action Breakdown'' poster-style storyboard. The layout should be a square 4x4 sixteen-grid arrangement, with each grid showing a continuous action step of the same street freestyle football performer in the same scene. The entire image should look like a combination of a ''high-end sports poster + technical breakdown teaching board,'' possessing both visual impact and a clear sense of instructional action explanation. [Overall Setting] The theme is: Street freestyle football performance, not an official match, not shooting practice, nor a multiplayer competition, but a single performer completing a full set of continuous freestyle football moves. The overall atmosphere should include: street feel, urban feel, cinematic feel, athletic feel, cool, and rhythmic. The background is set in a small nighttime city street court or urban plaza football space, featuring graffiti walls, wire fences, distant building lights, streetlamps, slightly reflective ground; the environment should be unified with a street-style trendiness.', null, null, 'The background is set in a small nighttime city street court or urban plaza football space, featuring graffiti walls, wire fences, distant building lights, streetlamps, slightly reflective ground; the environment should be unified with a…', null, null, null, null, 'square, city street, plaza', null),
('APX-S-4194-2', 'APX-C-4194', 2, null, null, null, '[Character Requirements] The protagonist is a young, handsome male freestyle football expert, with a light, coordinated, and athletic physique, short black hair, a confident demeanor, and fluid, controlled movements. The 16 grids in the entire image must feature the same person; do not change people in each grid. He wears a football kit with a "cool" vibe, but the word "Champion" should not appear, nor should any specific country name. The clothing should feel like a jersey from a professional team. [Layout Requirements] The entire image is a 4x4 sixteen-grid, each grid must have: 1. Large step numbers (1-16) 2. Chinese action titles 3. 2-4 brief Chinese action key points 4. Clear full-body action of the character 5. Football trajectory arrows / footwork trajectory lines 6. The football must be clearly visible and positioned reasonably, not floating or disappearing. The overall font style should lean towards a sports poster aesthetic, clear and powerful, suitable for social media sharing.', null, null, '[Character Requirements] The protagonist is a young, handsome male freestyle football expert, with a light, coordinated, and athletic physique, short black hair, a confident demeanor, and fluid, controlled movements.', null, null, null, null, null, null),
('APX-S-4194-3', 'APX-C-4194', 3, null, null, null, 'The image should be sharp, clear, and clean; both the character and the football should be complete, no feet cut off. [Action Sequence] Please design 16 continuous actions in the following order, each action distinctly different, forming a complete freestyle performance flow: 1. Street Opening Pose Action: One foot on the ball, body open, confident stance, like the start of a performance. Points: Dominant stance / Right foot on ball / Showing confidence 2. Sole Roll-back Action: Roll the ball back with the sole of the foot, adding a slight lateral movement. Points: Sole on ball / Pull ball back / Slight body turn 3. Step-over Action: Both feet performing step-overs around the football. Points: One foot circling ball / Step over and switch feet / Smooth rhythm 4. Inside-Outside Dribble Action: Use the inside and outside of the foot to tap the ball continuously, switching left and right.', null, null, 'The image should be sharp, clear, and clean; both the character and the football should be complete, no feet cut off.', null, null, null, null, null, null),
('APX-S-4194-4', 'APX-C-4194', 4, null, null, null, 'Points: Inside touch / Outside touch / Quick switching 5. Laces Flick-up Action: Use the laces to flick the ball upward, lifting it off the ground. Points: Laces power / Flick ball up / Ball rises in front 6. Continuous Juggling Action: Continuous juggling with the laces, keeping the ball bouncing up and down in front of the body. Points: Alternate juggling / Keep rhythm / Stable continuity 7. Knee Control Action: Control the ball bounce using knees or thighs. Points: Ball hits knee / Control landing point / Maintain balance 8. Heel Flick Action: Use the heel to flick the ball up from behind or side-rear. Points: Heel contact / Flick upward / Lean body forward 9. Around the World (ATW) Action: One foot circles the airborne ball. Points: Foot circles outward / One full circle / Stable landing control 10. Crossover ATW Action: Cross legs to complete a circling trick. Points: Front leg cross / One full circle / Mid-air switch 11.', null, null, 'Points: Inside touch / Outside touch / Quick switching 5. Laces Flick-up Use the laces to flick the ball upward, lifting it off the ground. Points: Laces power / Flick ball up / Ball rises in front 6.', null, null, null, null, null, null),
('APX-S-4194-5', 'APX-C-4194', 5, null, null, null, 'Shoulder Stall Action: Stall the ball on the shoulder or near the neck. Points: Ball lands on shoulder / Tighten shoulder / Stable stall 12. Back Stall Action: Lean forward to let the ball stay briefly on the back. Points: Lean body forward / Ball on back / Maintain balance 13. Rainbow Flick Action: Flick the ball from behind over the head, forming a rainbow trajectory. Points: Heel flick / Ball over head / Arched trajectory 14. Spin and Catch Action: Spin in place and catch the falling ball. Points: In-place spin / Catch falling ball / Soft landing control 15. Toe Stall Action: Use the tip of the toe or the top of the shoe to precisely stop the ball. Points: Toe lift / Precise stall / Perfect balance 16. Street Curtain Call Action: One foot on the ball again, arms open, like the closing of a full performance. Points: Right foot on ball / Open arms / Stylish curtain call [Visual Style] - Overall high-end sports poster style - Cinematic night scene lighting - Strong sense of motion, with a bit of trendy street aesthetic - Arrows and trajectory lines must be clear to help understand the ball''s movement path - Color scheme mainly Red, Black, and Gold, highlighting high-end quality and Chinese Red vibe - Eye-catching fonts, suitable for Xiaohongshu / Twitter / social media sharing - The entire image should look like a complete "16-step freestyle football action storyboard poster"', null, null, 'Shoulder Stall Stall the ball on the shoulder or near the neck. Points: Ball lands on shoulder / Tighten shoulder / Stable stall 12. Back Stall Lean forward to let the ball stay briefly on the back.', null, null, null, null, null, null),
