('APX-S-4057-1', 'APX-C-4057', 1, null, null, null, 'follow this Story Board to create a AD. dynamic camera movement, no camera gear in the shots, only her, only text in the last scene story = a beautiful woman in a white dress enjoying a amazing sunset evening at a luxury mansion build into a cliff, Scenes: 1) wide angle drone shot 2) wide angle walk at pool 3) medium wide over shoulder walk at pool 4) medium wide lean on railing 5) close-up hand in water 6) look over bay 7) close-up smile 8) wide angle smile holding champagne with elegant font text "LuxLife Retreats"', null, null, 'Dynamic camera movement, no camera gear in the shots, only her, only text in the last scene story = a beautiful woman in a white dress enjoying a amazing sunset evening at a luxury mansion build into a cliff, Scenes: 1) 2) walk at pool 3)…', null, null, 'champagne', 'incidental', 'cliff', null),
('APX-S-4053-1', 'APX-C-4053', 1, null, null, null, null, 1, 596, 'Snowy Mount Fuji visible through a wooden window frame, cold blue moonlight slicing into warm lantern-lit interior. Comedic heist-turned-chaos mood: theatrical tension, sudden slapstick destruction, absurd tonal shifts.', 'agent', 'chopping', null, null, 'bedroom', 'comedic'),
('APX-S-4053-2', 'APX-C-4053', 2, null, null, null, 'No gore, no real harm. Dynamic camera: voyeuristic framing, POV sweeps, low-angle impacts, dramatic zooms, stylized slow-motion beats, split-screen reaction with debris. Ultra-smooth motion, sharp comedic timing, vintage film grain overlay, implied exaggerated foley (wood cracks, fabric swish, dramatic gasps, metallic sparkle chimes). Characters 1. Orange cat thief: slim, agile, sly expression, wearing a loose gray Taoist robe. Movements stealthy but slightly overconfident, feline precision with theatrical flair.', null, null, 'Dynamic camera: voyeuristic framing, POV sweeps, low-angle impacts, dramatic, stylized beats, split-screen reaction with debris.', 'agent', null, null, null, null, 'comedic'),
('APX-S-4053-3', 'APX-C-4053', 3, null, null, null, '2. White cat: elegant, curvy silhouette, pink kimono, pale purple eyeshadow, vivid red lips. Sleeps dramatically, snores softly, then shifts to exaggerated panic and later glamorous poise. 3. Black bear: large, muscular, wearing a red dudou (belly garment), wielding a crude wooden stick. Movements heavy, explosive, wildly inaccurate but powerful. 4. Background townsfolk: gray rabbits in rough cloth garments, curious, reactive. Sequence (0:00–0:15) 0:00–0:01.1 close-up exterior: orange cat crouches outside wooden window, snow drifting.', null, null, 'White cat: elegant, curvy silhouette, pink kimono, pale purple eyeshadow, vivid lips. Sleeps dramatically, snores softly, then shifts to exaggerated panic and later glamorous poise.', 'animal-character', null, null, null, null, 'intense'),
('APX-S-4053-4', 'APX-C-4053', 4, null, null, null, 'Fuji glows. Cat whispers: “Jackpot night.” Eyes narrow. 0:01.1–0:02.2 POV sweep: rapid scan across dark tatami room, shadows sliding past like brush strokes. 0:02.2–0:03.2 POV hold: white cat sleeping under blanket, soft snoring. Subtle comedic snore bubble. 0:03.2–0:04.2 POV shift: gaze lands on low table—golden beckoning cat statue gleams under lantern light, tiny sparkle pulse. 0:04.2–0:05.0 close-up: orange cat’s lower face, slow crooked grin. “Mine.” 0:05.0–0:06.2 medium: orange cat slips through window silently, lands, pads forward in exaggerated tiptoe, robe swaying.', null, null, 'Cat whispers: “Jackpot night.” Eyes narrow. 1–.2 POV sweep: rapid scan across dark tatami room, shadows sliding past like brush strokes. 2–.2 POV hold: white cat sleeping under blanket, soft snoring. Subtle comedic snore bubble.', 'animal-character', 'sliding', null, null, null, 'comedic'),
('APX-S-4053-5', 'APX-C-4053', 5, null, null, null, '0:06.2–0:07.0 detail: as cat kneels and reaches—his foot accidentally nudges the white cat’s blanket. Fabric shifts. Suspense beat. 0:07.0–0:07.8 snap close-up: white cat’s eyes burst open. Sharp inhale. 0:07.8–0:08.6 scream: “THIEF! HELP!!” echoing dramatically. 0:08.6–0:10.0 chaos burst: flimsy wooden door slams open. Black bear charges in yelling: “WHERE?!” swings stick wildly—smashes table edge, wall panels, lantern stand. Orange cat dodges in fluid arcs. White cat scrambles to corner, shrieking.', null, null, '2–.0 as cat kneels and reaches—his foot accidentally nudges the white cat’s blanket.', 'agent', null, null, null, null, null),
('APX-S-4053-6', 'APX-C-4053', 6, null, null, null, null, 2748, 146, '0–.0 impact: black bear’s stick slams directly into the golden beckoning cat statue—it explodes into flying golden shards, fr.', 'animal-character', null, null, null, null, null)
) as v(shot_id, clip_id, shot_index, tc_in, tc_out, duration_s, verbatim_literal,
       slice_at, slice_len, description, subject_role, action, food_item,
       food_role, setting, mood)
join clips c on c.clip_id = v.clip_id
-- The clip insert above is DO NOTHING, so for a clip that ALREADY existed
-- its row still holds the original shot_count and the original shots. Without
-- this guard the shot insert would still run for it, and wherever this
-- splitter finds more beats than the original decomposition did, the extra
-- higher-index shots would land on top — leaving one clip carrying two
-- different decompositions at once (28 clips, 44 stray shots, seen for real).
-- For a clip this load actually inserted, shot_count is this run's own count,
-- so every shot passes.
where v.shot_index::int <= c.shot_count
-- Same reasoning as the clips: never touch a shot that already exists.
on conflict (shot_id) do nothing;
